#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, a pigeon came from Bari, with a letter from Luka, the ship's boy!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Capitão|Capitã|Capitães|Capitãs}, chegou um pombo de Bari, com uma carta do Luka, o grumete!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He writes: \"A Count has come to Italy, Count Malvento. He shows a Golden Charter.\""
msgstr "Ele escreve: «Chegou a Itália um Conde, o Conde Malvento. Mostra uma Carta Dourada.»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"He takes a toll in every harbour, from Comacchio to Otranto!\""
msgstr "«Cobra uma portagem em todos os portos, de Comacchio a Otranto!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"His men even took the eel nets of Comacchio as a toll. Please help!\""
msgstr "«Os homens dele até levaram as redes das enguias de Comacchio como portagem. Ajudem!»"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Count's men with the eel nets?"
msgstr "Viram os homens do Conde com as redes das enguias?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which boat is the Count's? Remember its sail and its hull!"
msgstr "Qual é o barco do Conde? Lembrem-se da vela e do casco!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres data/missions/26_caps_too_new/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, not this one! Think of the sail and the hull."
msgstr "Não, este não! Pensem na vela e no casco."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"That's the one! The Count's men shrug: \"The Count says nets are a toll.\" But they give them "
"back."
msgstr ""
"É esse! Os homens do Conde encolhem os ombros: «O Conde diz que as redes são portagem.» Mas "
"devolvem-nas."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the eel nets home to {port}."
msgstr "Levem as redes das enguias de volta {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our nets! Now we can catch the eels again."
msgstr "As nossas redes! Agora podemos voltar a apanhar enguias."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tonight, the whole lagoon eats eels!"
msgstr "Esta noite, a laguna inteira come enguias!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But this Count... Nobody here ever heard of him before."
msgstr "Mas este Conde... Ninguém aqui tinha ouvido falar dele."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Who is he really, captain?"
msgstr "Quem é ele, afinal, {crew|capitão|capitã|capitães|capitãs}?"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nets of Comacchio"
msgstr "As Redes de Comacchio"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first crossing to Italy. The Count's men took the eel nets of Comacchio \"as a toll\". Follow "
"their boat and give the nets back."
msgstr ""
"A primeira travessia para Itália. Os homens do Conde levaram as redes das enguias de Comacchio "
"«como portagem». Sigam o barco deles e devolvam as redes."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The eels of Comacchio are born far away, in the Sargasso Sea across the ocean, and swim all the "
"way to the lagoon. Nobody knew it in 1600: it was found out only around 1920."
msgstr ""
"As enguias de Comacchio nascem muito longe, no mar dos Sargaços, do outro lado do oceano, e nadam "
"até à laguna. Em 1600 ninguém sabia: só se descobriu por volta de 1920."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The nets are home!"
msgstr "As redes voltaram!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You crossed the sea and found the Count's boat."
msgstr "Atravessaram o mar e encontraram o barco do Conde."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/16_nets_of_comacchio/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The eel fishers of Comacchio can fish again."
msgstr "Os pescadores de enguias de Comacchio já podem voltar a pescar."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/17_wind_seller/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count sells \"wind charms\" to the fishermen of this coast."
